From 1bcbaac0bf12fd0f040c41814c83b1c0988d562a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sanju Abraham <s.abraham@f5.com>
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 12:33:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] feat(governance): test fixture mock + schema excludes for
 User CRUD

Closes two gaps where patch1's earlier patches extend the ConfigStore
interface and Go struct fields but leave the upstream test fixtures
out of sync, causing make test (and the TestConfigSchemaSync test) to
fail once patches are applied:

  1. MockConfigStore in transports/bifrost-http/lib/config_test.go now
     implements the six User CRUD methods added to the ConfigStore
     interface by 0001 + 0003 (GetUsers, GetUser, GetUsersPaginated,
     CreateUser, UpdateUser, DeleteUser). The mock stubs return empty
     values - bifrost-http/lib tests don't exercise user governance
     directly, but the type assertion via *MockConfigStore as
     configstore.ConfigStore must still satisfy.

  2. excludedGoFields in TestConfigSchemaSync now covers the new
     fields patch1 added without a matching entry in
     config.schema.json:

       - GovernanceConfig.users (added by 0001)
       - TableVirtualKey.user_id + .user (added by 0002)
       - TableBudget.user_id (added by 0001)
       - TableTeam.source_id (added by 0001)

     These are managed via the user-governance API rather than
     config.json - same rationale as model_configs / providers /
     routing_rules already in the exclude list.

With this patch applied on top of the other 7, make test passes 922
unit tests with 0 failures.
